# Mockup first (same palette)

When creating **any new frontend screen** (page, route, modal-as-screen, major view):

1. **Do not** implement production UI first.
2. **Extract** the existing frontend palette (CSS variables, theme tokens, Tailwind theme, or shared styles). Reuse those colors — do not invent a new palette.
3. **Create a mockup first** — lightweight HTML/CSS or a clearly named throwaway route/file (e.g. `mockups/<screen>.html` or `app/(mockups)/…`) using the **same** colors, type scale, and spacing tokens as the live app.
4. Show the mockup to the user and wait for approval (or explicit “skip mockup”).
5. Only then implement the real screen, still on the same palette tokens.

Also load `hallmark` + `frontend-design` for visual work. Use MCP `inspo` when picking a vibe. Skip this gate only for pure logic/data changes with no new visual surface, or when the user explicitly skips the mockup.
